## 2. GGUF Split: Reject a Shard Whose `split.no` Is Out of Range

**Component:** `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — `gguf_split_paths()`

**Responsibilities:** Resolves any shard path of a split model into the ordered list of all shard paths, verifying each file exists.

**Problem:** The function validates `no >= 1 && no <= n` for the *input* shard, but does not check that the resolved filenames for shards 2..N actually parse back to the same `n`. A file named `model-00001-of-00004.gguf` alongside `model-00002-of-00005.gguf` (a rename accident) would be silently accepted as a 4-shard model because only the input's digits are checked.

**Proposed change:** After building the path list, re-parse each generated path's `-of-` suffix and confirm the total matches.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -42,6 +42,14 @@ inline std::vector<std::string> gguf_split_paths(const std::string& any) {
         if (!std::ifstream(p, std::ios::binary))
             throw std::runtime_error("missing model shard " + p + " (shard " + std::to_string(i) + " of " +
                                      std::to_string(n) + "; is the download complete?)");
+        // Re-parse the generated name to confirm the total digits survived the replace (a path with
+        // embedded digits in the directory name could confuse a naive caller).
+        const size_t chk = p.rfind(tag);
+        if (chk == std::string::npos || p.size() != chk + 4 + 5 + 5 || p.compare(chk + 9, 5, ".gguf") != 0)
+            throw std::runtime_error("gguf_split_paths: generated path '" + p + "' does not end in -NNNNN-of-MMMMM.gguf");
+        int chk_n = 0;
+        for (size_t d = 0; d < 5; ++d) chk_n = chk_n * 10 + (p[chk + 4 + d] - '0');
+        if (chk_n != n) throw std::runtime_error("gguf_split_paths: shard " + p + " declares total " + std::to_string(chk_n) + ", expected " + std::to_string(n));
         out.push_back(std::move(p));
     }
     return out;
```

**Verification cases:**
1. **Mismatched total:** Create files `x-00001-of-00004.gguf` and `x-00002-of-00004.gguf` (only 2 of 4 exist). Call with shard 1's path. Must throw "missing model shard" naming shard 3.
2. **Directory with digits:** Place valid 2-shard files under `./2024/model-00001-of-00002.gguf`. Call with that path. Must succeed and return both paths in order.

